  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assistance alimentaire et nutritionnelle au Niger et service a&#xE9;rien humanitaire des Nations Unies</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this WFP project is to provide emergency food assistance through general food and cash distributions for 3 months to the targeted people, and to provide safe, reliable, efficient humanitarian transport to for people and light cargo. The project provides food assistance to 16,402 people identified as highly food insecure, prevention and management of moderate acute malnutrition in 13,016 children aged 6 to 23 months and transportation for 1,130 workers and 1.8MT of light freight for humanitarian entities, including MEDEVAC capacity. The intervention provides humanitarian assistance to 16,402 people (3,424 men, 3,465 women and 9,513 children), including 690 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
